(7300229, 1137696, 121111, '<td valign="top">Thanks again ! <br/> <br/>The trees are called "Sabino"<br/> <br/>How far from the original ? you mean how much editing ? Light was extreme, so it was a good candidate for HDR, although I processed a single RAW, the SOOC is way to dark as I picked the one where the highlights were manageable.<br/> <br/>LR gave decent results with highlights -100, exposure +1 , shadows +100<br/>gradient filter on the bottom to add clarity and a bit more exposure<br/>gradient on top to add contrast and saturation <br/> <br/>wish I had used a speed of 1/125 to freeze the ducks, I think I had a 3 stop ND and ISO 50 , so there was more than enough light to do it ... <br/> <br/>The lake is quite pretty to visit when there is no one around, like 6AM :) around lunch time it gets crowded, there are boat rides, food vendors, music, a 180 degree turn from the mood shown here. There is a hotel that looks decent right outside the park. <br/></td>', 'Thanks again !  The trees are called "Sabino" How far from the original ? you mean how much editing ? Light was extreme, so it was a good candidate for HDR, although I processed a single RAW, the SOOC is way to dark as I picked the one where the highlights were manageable. LR gave decent results with highlights -100, exposure +1 , shadows +100gradient filter on the bottom to add clarity and a bit more exposuregradient on top to add contrast and saturation  wish I had used a speed of 1/125 to freeze the ducks, I think I had a 3 stop ND and ISO 50 , so there was more than enough light to do it ...  The lake is quite pretty to visit when there is no one around, like 6AM :) around lunch time it gets crowded, there are boat rides, food vendors, music, a 180 degree turn from the mood shown here. There is a hotel that looks decent right outside the park. ', '2015-01-08 11:54:52.000000', NULL, 0),
