(7300268, 1137915, 13077, '<td valign="top">I think what he meant was that this photo offers only face value. Nothing open to interpretation or imagination.<br/> <br/>It''s a genre not everyone likes, which would account for some of the lower votes I guess. Still, 6 and higher would mean those voters thought it above average.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote this one but I would have given it a 6 for the pose, light and fairly clean background. The focus does look like it was pretty far behind the buck, though. Had it been on the head, I would say at least a 7.</td>', 'I think what he meant was that this photo offers only face value. Nothing open to interpretation or imagination. It''s a genre not everyone likes, which would account for some of the lower votes I guess. Still, 6 and higher would mean those voters thought it above average. I didn''t vote this one but I would have given it a 6 for the pose, light and fairly clean background. The focus does look like it was pretty far behind the buck, though. Had it been on the head, I would say at least a 7.', '2015-01-08 13:27:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7300276, 1138146, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MadMan2k:</b></div><hr/><i> A very interesting shape and texture study. I disagree with the need for wider DOF, I think this amount is optimal. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, Jon.  Yeah, I don''t agree with the need for more DoF either - there''s plenty there.  I have to be honest and say I''m quite disappointed with the way this scored and I suspect that it suffered at the hand of the auto-resizing on verticals as much of the detail was lost at voting size.  The crop is rather tight, but that''s the way it was straight out of camera.  I have a personal version with more room added right and left and I suspect that the added space might have helped it somewhat, but it would have violated the editing rules.  Perhaps I should have added a black frame that was wider at the sides - people wouldn''t have noticed it wasn''t part of the shot.  LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by MadMan2k: A very interesting shape and texture study. I disagree with the need for wider DOF, I think this amount is optimal.   Thanks, Jon.  Yeah, I don''t agree with the need for more DoF either - there''s plenty there.  I have to be honest and say I''m quite disappointed with the way this scored and I suspect that it suffered at the hand of the auto-resizing on verticals as much of the detail was lost at voting size.  The crop is rather tight, but that''s the way it was straight out of camera.  I have a personal version with more room added right and left and I suspect that the added space might have helped it somewhat, but it would have violated the editing rules.  Perhaps I should have added a black frame that was wider at the sides - people wouldn''t have noticed it wasn''t part of the shot.  LOL', '2015-01-08 13:37:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7300280, 1138061, 173844, '<td valign="top">I didn''t really "see" this gentleman''s face, partially hidden by the sunburst, and now I wish I had rated it 2 or 3 points higher.  Sorry.</td>', 'I didn''t really "see" this gentleman''s face, partially hidden by the sunburst, and now I wish I had rated it 2 or 3 points higher.  Sorry.', '2015-01-08 13:55:35.000000', NULL, 0),
